@startuml ehds-incident-coordination
' Rendered by scripts/render-plantuml.sh into docs/security/img/.
title Incident coordination between the parties: who notifies whom, and the clocks

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #64748B
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFFBEB
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #D97706
skinparam ActivityStartColor #059669
skinparam ActivityEndColor #059669
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontStyle bold
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #94A3B8

|#F8FAFC|Operating company (security operations)|
start
:Alert from the SIEM, or a report from a party
(a data user must report its own breach at once, Art. 61);
:Triages within the hour: scope,
data categories, parties affected;
:Contains: revokes credentials, isolates
the connector or the SPE session;
fork
  if (Personal data affected?) then (yes)
    |#FFF7ED|Controller: access body (SPE, permits) or holder (its data)|
    :Is informed without undue delay;
    if (Likely risk to the persons' rights?) then (yes)
      #FEF2F2:Notifies the data protection authority
      within 72 hours (GDPR Art. 33);
      #FEF2F2:Informs the persons without
      undue delay (GDPR Art. 34);
    else (no)
      :Records the breach internally
      (GDPR Art. 33(5));
    endif
  else (no)
  endif
fork again
  |Operating company (security operations)|
  if (Significant incident? (NIS2 as transposed)) then (yes)
    |#F1F5F9|BSI, national CSIRT|
    #FEF2F2:Receives the early warning
    within 24 hours;
    #FEF2F2:Receives the incident notification
    within 72 hours;
    #FEF2F2:Receives the final report
    within one month;
  else (no)
  endif
fork again
  |Operating company (security operations)|
  if (Data used outside the permit?) then (yes)
    |Controller: access body (SPE, permits) or holder (its data)|
    #FEF2F2:Revokes the permit, stops the processing
    without undue delay (EHDS Art. 63(2));
    :Informs the supervisory authority
    immediately if a GDPR breach is possible (Art. 63(2));
    |#FDF2F8|Health data user|
    :Loses access to the SPE until
    the access body decides;
  else (no)
  endif
fork again
  :Informs the affected holders in parallel;
  |#EEF2FF|Affected health data holders|
  :May suspend provision
  until the cause is known;
end fork
|Operating company (security operations)|
:Preserves the evidence: audit trail,
SIEM export, connector logs;
:Fixes, redeploys through the gated
pipeline, verifies the fix;
:Post-incident report, lessons learned,
an ADR where a decision changed;
|Controller: access body (SPE, permits) or holder (its data)|
:Corrective action where an SPE audit
found the cause (Art. 73(3));
stop

legend right
  The clocks are owned by role: the controller owns the GDPR ones,
  the operator the NIS2 ones, the access body the EHDS ones. The
  incident procedure names a person and a deputy for each lane; the
  tabletop exercise before go-live walks this diagram once.
endlegend
@enduml
